# Package Management

## Install a package

```bash
ansible all -b -m apt -a "name=nginx state=present"
```

## Install multiple packages

```bash
ansible all -b -m apt -a "name=git,curl,wget state=present"
```

## Update package cache

```bash
ansible all -b -m apt -a "update_cache=yes"
```

## Upgrade installed packages

```bash
ansible all -b -m apt -a "upgrade=yes"
```

## Remove a package

```bash
ansible all -b -m apt -a "name=apache2 state=absent"
```

## Completely remove a package

```bash
ansible all -b -m apt -a "name=apache2 state=purged"
```

## Install the latest package version

```bash
ansible all -b -m apt -a "name=docker.io state=latest"
```

## Install packages on a specific group

```bash
ansible webservers -b -m apt -a "name=nginx state=present"
```

## Install package using yum (RHEL/CentOS)

```bash
ansible all -b -m yum -a "name=httpd state=present"
```

## Install package using package module

```bash
ansible all -b -m package -a "name=vim state=present"
```
